From: OpenAI Codex <codex@openai.com>
Subject: [PATCH] survive: mirror a quarter-turn roll at each emulated wrist

Apply the requested right-clockwise and left-counterclockwise 90 degree roll
in wrist-local space. Retain the derived wrist position and its velocities,
so the adjustment changes hand orientation without moving the wrist anchor.

diff --git a/src/xrt/drivers/survive/survive_driver.c b/src/xrt/drivers/survive/survive_driver.c
--- a/src/xrt/drivers/survive/survive_driver.c
+++ b/src/xrt/drivers/survive/survive_driver.c
@@ -470,6 +470,13 @@
 	m_relation_chain_push_pose(&chain, &survive->imu_from_head);
 	m_relation_chain_push_relation(&chain, &hand_relation);
 	m_relation_chain_resolve(&chain, &out_value->hand_pose);
+
+	// Roll the simulated hand about its local finger direction (-Z), keeping
+	// the wrist origin fixed. Right is clockwise, left is its mirror image.
+	const float half_sqrt = sqrtf(0.5f);
+	struct xrt_quat wrist_roll = {.z = left ? half_sqrt : -half_sqrt, .w = half_sqrt};
+	math_quat_rotate(&out_value->hand_pose.pose.orientation, &wrist_roll,
+	                 &out_value->hand_pose.pose.orientation);
 
 	// This is the truth - we pose-predicted or interpolated all the way up to `at_timestamp_ns`.
 	*out_timestamp_ns = at_timestamp_ns;
